      <div type="clause" n="31">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 31</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>XXVI. Gif he sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.12"/> twelfhynde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.19"/>, ælc hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.20"/> hundtwelftig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.star3"/> scill., se slaga wer ⁊ wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>XXV. Gif he sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.4"/> XII hynde, ælc heora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.7"/> CXX scill', ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.3"/> se slaga wer ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.3"/> wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>Be twylfhendu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> m<hi rend="italic">en</hi>. Gyf he sy twelfhynde, ælc heora hundtwelftig scill',<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.3-2"/> se slaga wér ⁊ wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.10"/> twelfhind<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.11"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.8"/> sit, quotquot interfuerint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.12-2"/> CXX sol. reddant, et occisor weram<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_31.lnote.oe.13"/> et witam.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="76" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be twylfhendum men.] Gif he sie twelfhynde<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#Af_31.attnote.fn.8"/>, ælc hiora hundtwelftig scill. [geselle, ⁊]<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Af_31.attnote.fn.9"/> se<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Af_31.attnote.fn.10"/> slaga wer ⁊ wite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="30.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="322" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXVI} Gif he sie twelfhynde, ælc hiora hundtwelftig scill, se slaga wer ⁊ wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn der [Erschlagene] 1200<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_31.lnote.de.1"/> [Schilling werth] ist, [zahle] jeder von jenen [Begleitern] 120 Schilling, der Todtschläger [selbst] Wergeld und Strafgeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If the [slain man] is [worth] 1200 [shillings], [let] each of those [companions pay] 120 shillings, the slayer [himself] the wergeld and the fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="77" ed="#attenborough"/>If the wergeld of the slain man is 1200 shillings, each of them [shall pay] 120 shillings; and the homicide [shall pay] the wergeld and the fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="413" ed="#whitelock"/>If he is a man of a twelve-hundred wergild, each of them [is to pay] 120 shillings, and the slayer the wergild and the fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="323" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If he should be [a] 1,200-[wergild man], each of [the members of the band] 120 shillings, the slayer <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> and fine.</ab>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">Whitelock numbers this chapter 31 and gives Liebermann’s number, 31, in brackets.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man added by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heora <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heora So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hundtwelftigum scill' geselle [h. sc. agyfe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi>] ⁊ se slaga were <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hundtwelftigum scill' geselle [h. sc. agyfe Ld] ⁊ se slaga were So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eo <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eo on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">homo <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">homo added by Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond Hn;</hi> man <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Or;</hi> duodecimhindus <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond Hn; man added by Or; duodecimhindus the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-hyn. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> -hun. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-hyn. T; -hun. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.12-2" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-runt <hi rend="italic">Lond T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-runt Lond T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wi. et we. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wi. et we. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ <hi rend="italic">fügt spätere Hd. hinzu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ added by a later hand</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_31.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> o. zu Rb 29. Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> wie Hn 87, 4 behält das Agsä. Wort bei, das spätere Rez. latinisiert. Mit Recht identifiziert Inst. (auch zu 39, 2) den 1200 Schilling-Mann mit dem Thegn; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 13a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> above on Rb 29. Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>, like Hn 87, 4, keeps the A.-S. word, which the later recension latinizes. Inst. (also on 39, 2) rightly identifies the 1200-shilling man with the thegn; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 13a</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_31.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>twelfhynde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Ld. adds <hi rend="italic">man</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_31.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>⁊</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hundtwelftigum scill' geselle</hi> [<hi rend="italic">h. sc. agyfe</hi>. Ld] ⁊ <hi rend="italic">se slaga were</hi>. So, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_31.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>se</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ond se</hi>. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
